Third-party data attributions
=============================

This application and its curriculum build pipeline use the following
open-licensed data sources. The compiled curriculum database
(mobile/assets/curriculum-seed/curriculum.db and OTA updates of it) contains
data derived from them. This file is the repository-level attribution required
by their licenses; the app additionally surfaces these attributions in
Settings → About.

EDRDG dictionary files: JMdict, KANJIDIC2, KRADFILE
---------------------------------------------------
This project uses the JMdict, KANJIDIC2, and KRADFILE/RADKFILE dictionary
files. These files are the property of the Electronic Dictionary Research and
Development Group (EDRDG), and are used in conformance with the Group's
licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
(CC BY-SA 4.0).

  https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Used for: verifying and correcting kanji readings/meanings, vocabulary
glosses/readings, and kanji component decompositions in curriculum/ (see
curriculum/_build/import/). Corrected facts derived from these files ship in
the curriculum database.

JmdictFurigana
--------------
Furigana annotations in the curriculum (bracket-notation readings on
vocabulary, example sentences, and reading passages) are derived from the
JmdictFurigana project by Doublevil, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0. JmdictFurigana is
itself derived from the EDRDG's JMdict.

  https://github.com/Doublevil/JmdictFurigana
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

